Ours (dsv41 recipe), Apache-2.0, against vLLM main 6e517b15 + patches 0001-0018.
Short-context CUDA graph twins for DeepSeek-V4.1's sparse indexer (VLLM_SHORT_CTX_BOUNDS="512,1025" for V4.1; off when
unset). Below index_topk compressed entries the indexer selects every entry, and V4.1 already skips its scoring then
(wq_b GEMM, logits, candidate masks, top-k: _fill_short_context_topk_indices), but only eagerly: inside a CUDA graph the
branch is never taken, so every decode step scores. On 2x GB10 the 8 scoring layers cost +133 us each over a plain
layer at k=5 (LOG Oct 11 06:27), ~1.2 ms a verify round, for contexts where the result is "all entries".
With bounds set, each FULL decode graph of the target model gets a twin per bound, captured with the bound published
(vllm/v1/worker/gpu/short_ctx.py), so the indexer takes its short branch in the layers whose ratio allows it
(bound // compress_ratio <= index_topk); the runner sets the batch's longest sequence after the step (+ a margin,
VLLM_SHORT_CTX_MARGIN, 16) before dispatch, and dispatch picks the smallest covering twin; batches with a prefill, or
longer contexts, keep the normal graphs. The short branch selects the same entries in index order rather than score
order, so attention sums them in a different order (rounding only).

